From 0cf6d4528b6b902417151cdf6b3413f6d6455d07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:43:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: S-X8 q8_1 mat-vec ships OPT-IN, GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=1
 (R46 commit C decision)

Commit C admitted GGML_TYPE_SX8 in ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq() at every width, with its own
comment saying any width that loses at op level must be excluded before it ships. The paired
measurement says the losing widths do not form a shippable default.

RIG-A, test-backend-ops, 3 interleaved rounds per arm in one quiet hold, base = the unchanged
kernel (32-paired-c.txt, 96 cells). Against the SHIPPED kernel the q8_1 path loses at n=7 on
three of the four primary 27B shapes: -28.37% (4096x14336), -26.13% (17408x5120), -13.29%
(5120x17408), raw rounds non-overlapping, so repeatable. The PREREG promotion bar (>5% median
at n=1..4, no >3% repeatable regression on any primary shape) is also missed at n=4,
4096x14336: -6.85% against the gated whole-block decode of commit B2.

Where it wins it wins large: +38.00/+45.73/+46.43/+51.79% at n=1..4 on 248320x5120, the
embed/output shape where B2's n<=3 gate hands wide batches back to the per-position kernel.
So the path is KEPT and reachable rather than deleted. It is not made default by a per-width
admit either: the winning region is one shape at two widths, and a threshold fitted to that is
overfitting, not routing. The n=7 cliff is non-monotonic (+13.69/-13.88/+17.68% at n=6/7/8 on
5120x17408 against B2), which points at a NUM_COLS == 7 tail defect in the mmvq framework
rather than a tuning loss; a narrowed admit must start there.

Precedent for shipping a measured win OFF until it is cleared: GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ, in the
same function.

Routing PROVEN in both directions, not assumed. A planted-RED in commit C's dot product only
(mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl, * 1.05), one binary: with the env unset all 12 sx8 MUL_MAT cases are
OK (40-correct-cg-red-off-MUL_MAT.txt); with GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=1 ten go red at ERR 0.00227
and only the two mul_mm cases (n=9 k=256, m=1 n=64) stay OK (40-correct-cg-red-on-MUL_MAT.txt).
RED reverted and rebuilt: MUL_MAT 13/13 OK, MUL_MAT_ID 3/3, GET_ROWS, CPY, 2/2 backends passed
in BOTH env arms. test-quantize-fns keeps the same 6 pre-existing failures (q2_0_g128,
q3_0_rocmfpx, q2_0_rocmfpx), no sx8 row.

arifi-sync-check rc=0. No default moves for any other type.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
WI: WI-1729
Lane: lane-230
